intent: >
  Wire bin/dot into a single OS-aware orchestration of all topic installers, and
  give docker/databases real Ubuntu branches — making the stack runnable end-to-end.
slice: "3/6"
kind: feature
behavior_change: additive
reversibility: reversible
scope:
  declared:
    - bin/dot
    - docker/install.sh
    - databases/install.sh
  actual:
    - bin/dot
    - docker/install.sh
    - databases/install.sh
  drift: []
proof:
  tests_run: "sh -n bin/dot; zsh -n docker/install.sh databases/install.sh; shellcheck -s sh bin/dot; dry dispatch/ordering check"
  result: green
  failing: 0
tests:
  needed: "no"
  rationale: >
    No suite. bin/dot shellcheck-clean (sh); docker/databases pass zsh -n. Verified
    the run() ordering (python before infra) and the macOS-only guards (defaults,
    iOS) via a dry dispatch. The real flow was NOT executed (it installs Docker
    Engine, apt packages, brew casks) — end-to-end is the Ubuntu VM / fresh-Mac step.
lint:
  run: "shellcheck -s sh bin/dot"
  result: clean
  count: 0
verification:
  tested:
    - "bin/dot shellcheck-clean; docker/databases zsh -n clean"
    - "Step ordering and macOS-only guards verified by dry dispatch"
  manual:
    - "Full bin/dot run NOT executed (installs real packages) — VM/fresh-Mac is the gate"
assumptions:
  - "Invoking installers with `zsh`/`bash`/`sh` explicitly (not the executable bit) is correct and portable"
  - "Docker apt repo + docker group is the right Ubuntu Docker path; group needs a re-login"
  - "apt mysql-server/postgresql/redis-server/memcached is the intended Ubuntu DB strategy (systemd)"
specifications:
  - "bin/dot order: packages -> macOS defaults(mac) -> ruby -> python -> node -> infra -> jvm -> php -> docker -> databases -> ios(mac) -> vim"
  - "Each step runs in its own interpreter; a failed step reports and continues (does not abort the run)"
  - "iOS and macOS-defaults steps are guarded Darwin-only"
deviations_from_plan: >
  "Fixed a latent bug while here (DNA-adjacent but worth calling out): the old bin/dot
  ran zsh installers via `sh`, mis-running zsh array indexing. Now each is invoked with
  its correct interpreter. Plan scope (bin/dot + docker + databases) otherwise unchanged."
trade_offs: >
  "Chose resilient orchestration (report-and-continue per step) over fail-fast so one
  broken installer doesn't block the rest during this transitional period — at the cost
  of a failed step being easy to miss in long output. Left ruby/node Ubuntu breakage to
  PR 4 (runtime modernization) rather than expanding this slice."
self_review:
  consistency: "docker/databases mirror the per-OS branch shape of the other topic installers; bin/dot keeps the #!/bin/sh + DOTHOME export convention."
  error_paths: "run() swallows per-step failure with a visible '!! failed' line; docker/db installers set -e and exit 1 on unsupported OS / missing Homebrew."
  security: "Docker apt key fetched over https into /etc/apt/keyrings with signed-by= in the source line; no unsigned apt."
  api: "bin/dot is the public entrypoint (sourced by script/bootstrap); same source contract, expanded steps. No signature change."
  dead_code: "Old Darwin/Linux case/esac in bin/dot replaced wholesale; nothing orphaned."
confidence: medium
reviewer_attention:
  - "bin/dot:30-46 — the step list/order and per-step interpreter; this is the load-bearing orchestration"
  - "On Ubuntu, ruby + node steps will fail until PR 4 (openssl@1.1 paths / no nvm-on-Linux) — expected, flagged"
  - "docker/install.sh:20-34 — Ubuntu Docker repo + group add, unrun"
